            "review_title": "Review at Java Crawfish",
            "review_text": "t L\n3 contributions\n0\nDon't believe the trip advisor map, it's on 45 yen phu\nAug 2015 • Couples\nWent here last night, having read the reviews and seen the advertising.\nService was ok. Food ok. Nothing terrible, nothing amazing either when compared to the other local food on offer elsewhere. So trip advisor on the whole was about ratings right.\nChips on the table were stale which was a bad omen, squid appetizers were chewy (they need to add in a tea spoon of bi-carb when making them), and the crab claws were more work than necessary (get the chopper knife and just give it a good old whack, otherwise the sauce can't go in). On the sauce, just using Thai sweet chilli and drenching it, isn't really cooking, sorry guys but I think that's a fair assessment.\nPositives, prawns were cooked well, it was frequented by locals and had a buzz to it. As for the Decor, it was bright and interesting... That's about as polite as I'd put it.\nWas still wondering if the seafood spring rolls had any seafood in it, and the menu isn't geared for foodies. (It's pretty Chinese 80's, ie meat and repeat).\nBasically, it's a real fisherman's attempt at a restaurant that doesn't have the love of home cooking, or the art of creativity elsewhere, but if you're after a decent meal for a decent price, yeah it just scrapes itself over that line.\nRead more\nWritten August 31, 2015",
