            "review_title": "Review at Java Crawfish",
            "review_text": "blueoceanvn\n60 contributions\n0\nA poor mixture of Asian and Western food.\nOct 2014 • Friends\nGot a chance to lunch here on the occasion of some colleagues' birthday. We had 4 tables with a 9-plate set menu for each. It's worth noting before hand that the restaurant's special plate (crawfish) weren't included in the set. Yet, the set cost 250.000VND/pax (equivalent of $23US) for lunch, drinks not included.\n\nLocated on West lake side, the restaurant has an amazing view on the famous lake of the capital. Best seat would be outside on the edge of the lake, but a table on 1st floor is just as good, probably better on a rainy day.\n\nFood-wise, things are not so bright. Aside from the Tuna salad and the cream and butter oysters which feel like Western food, the other plates were pretty much Asian.. yet we had to serve ourselves with knife and fork on a plate.. As a result, everyone pretty much struggled with their meal.\n\nIn a table for six, each person would get one piece of food on each dish.. one deep-fried roll, one oyster, one butter-garlic shrimp, etc... For 250K/pax, it's quite pricey, IMO.\nBesides, most of the seafoods here are frozen food which gave me a blah taste. Because, as a local, I'm so used to having fresh food, even seafood, everyday. Of all their selection of seafoods, maybe only crawfish is acceptable as frozen food 'cos they have to import, the others are freshly available everyday in local markets.\n\nI hope things will get better on the next visit 'cos my wife insists on trying their crawfish at least once.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 22, 2014",
